      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Reproduction – Meaning and Importance"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Reproduction is classified into Asexual (single parent, no fusion of gametes) and Sexual (two parents, fusion of gametes).",
        "Male gametes (sperm) are produced via spermatogenesis in the seminiferous tubules of the testes.",
        "Female gametes (ova) are produced via oogenesis in the ovaries and released during ovulation.",
        "The menstrual cycle is regulated by pitutory hormones (FSH, LH) and ovarian hormones (Estrogen, Progesterone).",
        "Fertilization occurs in the fallopian tube, forming a zygote that implants into the uterine wall for pregnancy."
      ],
      "id": "kebq834"
