    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Fertilization occurs specifically in the ampullary region of the Fallopian tube (Oviduct).",
        "LH surge (rapid rise in Luteinizing Hormone) triggers ovulation around Day 14 of the menstrual cycle.",
        "Sertoli cells provide nourishment to developing sperm cells inside the testes.",
        "Human Chorionic Gonadotropin (hCG) is secreted by the placenta and detected in standard pregnancy test kits."
      ],
